From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wendy Labs <engineering@wendy.dev>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: iwlwifi: mld: advertise secure NAN capability

The driver implements NAN key handling but does not advertise SECURE_NAN.
Consequently nl80211_key_allowed() rejects NAN keys, and wpa_supplicant
2.12 fails NAN startup while installing its own IGTK.

Match the capability declaration in Intel's pinned backport driver. Set
it only when iwl_mld_nan_supported() enables NAN, preserving that function's
firmware command-version and NVM checks.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/iwlwifi/backport-iwlwifi/+/070e486a6d462c79bf6356832af28e45c1b94519/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/mac80211.c]
Signed-off-by: Wendy Labs <engineering@wendy.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/mac80211.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/mac80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/mac80211.c
@@ -271,6 +271,8 @@
 
 	hw->wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN);
 	hw->wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA);
+
+	wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SECURE_NAN);
 
 	hw->wiphy->nan_supported_bands = BIT(NL80211_BAND_2GHZ);
 	if (mld->nvm_data->bands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ].n_channels)
--
2.43.0
